Data sources (each technical specification field in the dataset records its own
source and license):

- Wikidata (https://www.wikidata.org) - structured data released under CC0 1.0.
- European Environment Agency (EEA) and Directorate-General for Climate Action
  (DG CLIMA), "Monitoring of CO2 emissions from passenger cars - Regulation (EU)
  2019/631", data for 2019 to 2025 (2019-2024 final, 2025 provisional) - reused
  under CC BY 4.0. Copyright holder: Directorate-General for Climate Action
  (DG-CLIMA). Source: European Environment Agency
  (https://www.eea.europa.eu/data-and-maps/data/co2-cars-emission-22).
  Data reported by EU Member States. The license (CC BY 4.0, "No limitations to
  public access") was checked on the metadata record of each year on 2026-09-20.
  Records are aggregated, merged across years and filtered by this project
  (category M1, Italy).
- RDW Open Data, "Gekentekende voertuigen" (https://opendata.rdw.nl) - Public
  Domain, attribution: Team Open Data RDW; license checked on 2026-09-20. Also the
  fuel table "Gekentekende voertuigen brandstof" (Public Domain, checked on
  2026-09-20). Used only to verify mass, engine size, wheelbase and engine power,
  aggregated by type, variant and version: no plate or other vehicle-level record
  is stored (a plate is held in memory during the build to look up its power, then
  discarded).

This project is not affiliated with, endorsed by or sponsored by any vehicle
manufacturer. Brand and model names are trademarks of their respective owners
and are used only to identify vehicles.

This file is updated whenever a source is added.
